# tests/mpx4-udp's run list (px22). kmain_sockets runs it from the
# initramfs as /etc/pax-run with tools/net-peer's UDP script at the
# other end of a socket netdev; tools/linux-net runs it on Linux with
# the same script at the other end of a tap device; the two outputs and
# exit statuses are compared byte for byte (but udpfill's and udphold's,
# whose answers are the receiving kernel's bounds: user/net/*.expect). One
# command a line, words separated by single spaces, the first the
# program's path. In order: what sockets answer with nothing on the
# wire; a client and a server over loopback; the echo server, asked by
# the script and then soaked; the client; the soak out; the echo server
# again for the wider battery; a queue filled from the wire; the
# resolver; a queue filled over loopback.
/bin/sockerr
/bin/udploop
/bin/udpecho 7 10.0.2.2 9099
/bin/udpclient 10.0.2.2 9099
/bin/udpsoak 10.0.2.2 9099 10000
/bin/udpecho 7 10.0.2.2 9098
/bin/udphold 4030 10.0.2.2 9097
/bin/resolve 10.0.2.3 pax.test
/bin/udpfill
